# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Computational cost (ms per MD step and atom) was measured for NVE MD of 16,000 atoms on 32 cores of an AMD Rome 7H12 node (Fig. 3b, figure-only).

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Training and test RMSEs are figure-only (Figs. 2-3, S2, S4) and the optimal hyperparameters are in SI Tables S1-S4; the text states only approximate values (all test energy RMSEs below 5 meV/atom, GAP about 2 meV/atom, force RMSEs about 0.04 eV/A, NNP about 0.06 eV/A).
# - The cutoff of 6.5 A is the stated default for all packages ('if not specified otherwise'). Dislocation core structures, Peierls barriers, double-kink energies (Table 2) and fracture behaviour are properties.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/zhang2024.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.
